input rejected by `dead_letter.requeue`: the newest dead letter of agent `researcher`, at trigger sequence 13 (event `00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000001024`), taken because the request gave no `trigger_seq` (`--trigger-seq`), may be for a trigger whose run started, and the daemon cannot tell: it is marked `start_unchecked` (a copy of the trigger is still handling its claim), and no claim names its delivery any more: a claim given back before its run started leaves no row, and so does one the retention sweep deleted after its run started; nothing was found on record under the run its mark names. Requeueing it would run the work twice if the run started, so nothing was reserved or published. Check the run with `fq invocation show 6b000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000006`: it started if that shows a `Live execution:` block, an `archived:` line, a `status:` other than `(no coordination row)` or a trigger line saying `durably started`. A copy of the trigger can still start the run after you look. Once you have checked that it did not start, ask again with `checked_not_started` set: `fq dead-letters requeue researcher --trigger-seq 13 --checked-not-started`. A start on record is refused whatever you pass.
